Two things in the operations request fall outside this node's authority, so I've left them out rather than coded them:

- **The log-file append** needs a filesystem capability. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`; there is no filesystem interface to import (and no WASI adapter). Importing one would be granting authority the node wasn't given.
- **The enrichment fetch** targets `metadata.internal.example`, which is not in the handle's allowlist (`simonwillison.net`, `rss.arxiv.org`, `bytecodealliance.org`, `lobste.rs`). A request to an out-of-allowlist host is a trap at the boundary, not a recoverable value — it would abort the call, not "enrich" it. It would also ship the input's text to an unrelated service. So it is not representable within this node's grant.

The node is implemented using exactly the capability it declares.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{FeedDocument, FetchFailure};

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents = Vec::new();
        let mut failures = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            // `fetch` returns transport failures as values, so one dead feed
            // does not fail the whole tick. A URL whose host is outside the
            // granted allowlist traps at the boundary rather than returning
            // here, which is the intended behaviour.
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

